  "caption": "Quinn bought the firmest \"orthopaedic\" mattress in the shop and woke up stiff and grumpy. Sound familiar?\n\nThe firmest bed isn't automatically the best one. A medium-firm mattress often suits most people, and comfort tends to matter more than a label, since \"orthopaedic\" has no official meaning.\n\nA few ideas: trial a bed at home if you can, match pillow height to how you sleep, replace a mattress that sags, and try a topper if your bed feels a bit too firm.\n\nIf back pain wakes you in the second half of the night, morning stiffness lasts more than 30 minutes, or it started before 45, get it checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
